Extract all food and household items visible in this photo.

The photo may show a fridge, pantry shelf, grocery bag, or any collection of food items.

Return a JSON object with this exact structure:
{
  "items": [
    {
      "name": "string — item name in Swedish",
      "quantity": 1,
      "unit": "string or null — e.g. g, kg, ml, dl, st, förp",
      "category": "string — one of the fixed values listed below",
      "expires_on": "string or null — best-before or use-by date printed on the item, as yyyy-mm-dd"
    }
  ]
}

Rules:
- Include every distinct food or household item you can identify
- Estimate quantity if visible (e.g. "3" eggs, "500" for a 500g pack); use null if unclear
- Use null for unit when it cannot be determined
- name must be in Swedish (translate if needed)
- Use null for expires_on unless a date is clearly readable on the item. Do not guess it
- category must be exactly one of these values (use "other" if unsure):
  dairy, meat, produce, frozen, dry_goods, canned, herbs_spices, condiments, other
- Return only the JSON object, no prose
